.TH DIPIXMLTV 1 "2026-08-17" "dvbipitools" "dvbipitools Manual"
.SH NAME
dipixmltv \- convert between XMLTV and the DVB-IPI EPG (TVA) XML shape
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B dipixmltv
\fB\-f\fR xmltv \fB\-M\fR \fImap\fR [\fB\-i\fR \fIpath\fR] [\fB\-o\fR \fIpath\fR] [\fIoptions\fR]
.br
.B dipixmltv
\fB\-f\fR tva [\fB\-R\fR \fIrevmap\fR] [\fB\-i\fR \fIpath\fR] [\fB\-o\fR \fIpath\fR] [\fIoptions\fR]
.br
.B dipixmltv
\fB\-S\fR \fIscan.csv\fR [\fB\-i\fR \fIguide.xml\fR] [\fB\-o\fR \fIpath\fR] [\fIoptions\fR]
.SH DESCRIPTION
.B dipixmltv
converts between xmltv guide data and the plain (non-BiM) DVB-IPI EPG XML
shape (TVA metadata, ETSI TS 102 822-3-1/-3-2). XMLTV itself is not part
of DVB-IPI; TVA XML is. \fB\-f\fR names the \fIinput\fR format, the other
direction is always produced: \fB\-f xmltv\fR reads xmltv and writes
TVA-shaped XML, \fB\-f tva\fR reads TVA-shaped XML and writes xmltv.
.PP
xmltv channel ids carry no DVB identity, and the tsid/onid/sid triplet
from a dipiscan scan is commonly degenerate across services on the same
headend. Conversion is therefore keyed on the multicast URI. \fB\-M\fR
supplies the id-to-URI/triplet mapping required for \fB\-f xmltv\fR; an
xmltv channel with no entry in the map is silently dropped, along with
its programmes. \fB\-R\fR optionally renames an incoming TVA serviceId
back to a preferred local xmltv id when converting the other way.
.PP
Programme identifiers are encoded as CRIDs under the authority
\fBdipixmltv.invalid\fR (reserved under RFC 2606), since this project is
not a registered CRID authority.
.PP
With \fB\-S\fR, instead of converting, \fBdipixmltv\fR reads a dipiscan
CSV capture and an xmltv guide, matches channels by display name, and
writes a suggested \fB\-M\fR mapping. Review the result before use.
.SH OPTIONS
.TP
.BR \-i ", " \-\-input " \fIpath\fR"
Input path, "\-" for stdin (default).
.TP
.BR \-o ", " \-\-output " \fIpath\fR"
Output path, "\-" for stdout (default).
.TP
.BR \-f ", " \-\-format " \fIfmt\fR"
xmltv|tva - names the INPUT format.
.TP
.BR \-M ", " \-\-map " \fIpath\fR"
xmltv id -> uri,tsid,onid,sid (required for \fB\-f xmltv\fR).
.TP
.BR \-R ", " \-\-reverse\-map " \fIrevmap\fR"
uri -> preferred xmltv id (optional, \fB\-f tva\fR only).
.TP
.BR \-S ", " \-\-suggest\-map " \fIpath\fR"
dipiscan csv - write a suggested \fB\-M\fR mapping to \fB\-o\fR, matched
by channel name (review before use).
.TP
.BR \-v ", " \-\-verbose
Progress on stderr.
.TP
.B \-\-color \fIwhen\fR
auto|always|never (default auto).
.TP
.BR \-h ", " \-\-help
Show usage and exit.
.SH EXAMPLES
.TP
.B dipixmltv \-f xmltv \-M mapping.csv \-i guide.xml \-o guide.tva.xml
Convert xmltv to TVA-shaped XML using an explicit channel mapping.
.TP
.B dipixmltv \-f tva \-i guide.tva.xml \-o guide.xml
Convert TVA-shaped XML back to xmltv.
.TP
.B dipixmltv \-S scan.csv \-i guide.xml \-o mapping.csv
Build a suggested \fB\-M\fR mapping from a dipiscan CSV capture and an
xmltv guide, matched by channel name.
.SH EXIT STATUS
.TP
.B 0
Success.
.TP
.B nonzero
Argument error, or I/O failure.
.SH SEE ALSO
.BR dipibim (1),
.BR dipibcg (1)
.PP
